upport.positive_curvature&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&ref=sha256%3A9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5%2Fnodes%2Fsupport.positive_curvature","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"Curated source-level mathematical statement, not an elaborated Lean extraction or independently accepted proof. Its displayed local hypotheses are quantified guards; a hypothetical plateau is not an added premise of the full-support theorem. Unconditional with respect to minimization; conditional on admissibility and a positive plateau. The cited Lean positive_gap_curvature supplies the positivity of the second derivative of curvatureMoment, not a claim of literal equality between every manuscript lemma and a Lean type.","citation_ids":["support_curvature_source","support_gap_lean_source"],"evidence_ids":["support_source_bindings_20261024","support_graph_semantic_review_pending"],"id":"support.positive_curvature","kind":"claim","label":"Strict curvature on a positive constant interval","locator":"curvature.tex:9–52; prop:gap-curvature","source_id":"support_tex_curvature","statement":"For every gamma in U and its controlled diffusion, if gamma=c>0 on an open interval I contained in (0,1), then q'''(t)>=(1/(1000*c^2))E[(cPhi_xx(t,X_t))^4]>0 for every t in I. Hence q' is strictly convex on I. The same local assertion applies to each interior point of (a,b) with 0<=a<b<1; the endpoints are reached by continuity of q'.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.positive_curvature","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity_at_jumps","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivi